{"key":"enterprise/T1090.001","id":"T1090.001","name":"Internal Proxy","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1090","tactics":["command-and-control"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may use an internal proxy to direct command and control traffic between two or more systems in a compromised environment. Many tools exist that enable traffic redirection through proxies or port redirection, including HTRAN, ZXProxy, and ZXPortMap. Adversaries use internal proxies to manage command and control communications inside a compromised environment, to reduce the number of simultaneous outbound network connections, to…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1090/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--f6dacc85-b37d-458e-b58d-74fc4bbf5755","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.724Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0051","name":"Firewall Rule Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0051","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d2ff4b56-8351-4ed8-b0fb-d8605366005f","page":"telemetry/DC0051/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacom